# TaskFlow REST API

A production-style RESTful task management API with JWT authentication, full CRUD operations, filtering/pagination, audit logging, and an integrated test suite. Zero external dependencies beyond Flask.

## Features
- **JWT auth from scratch** — HS256 tokens, no PyJWT needed
- **Full CRUD** — create, read, update (PATCH), delete tasks
- **Filtering** — by status, priority, free-text search
- **Pagination + sorting** — `page`, `per_page`, `sort`, `order`
- **Audit log** — every mutation tracked in `task_logs`
- **Input validation** — required fields, enum constraints, length limits
- **12 integration tests** — all passing

## Setup

```bash
pip install flask flask-cors
python app.py              # API on :5053
python app.py test         # run test suite (with server running)
```

## API Reference

### Auth
```
POST /auth/register    {"username","email","password"}
POST /auth/login       {"email","password"}
GET  /auth/me          (requires Bearer token)
```

### Tasks
```
GET    /tasks                         List (auth required)
       ?status=todo|in_progress|done  Filter by status
       ?priority=low|medium|high|urgent
       ?q=search+term                 Full-text search
       ?sort=created_at&order=desc    Sorting
       ?page=1&per_page=20            Pagination
POST   /tasks          {"title","description","status","priority","due_date","tags":[]}
GET    /tasks/<id>
PATCH  /tasks/<id>     (partial update any field)
DELETE /tasks/<id>
GET    /tasks/stats    Completion rate, by-status breakdown
GET    /tasks/<id>/logs  Audit trail
```

### Example

```bash
# Register
curl -X POST http://localhost:5053/auth/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username":"alice","email":"alice@example.com","password":"password123"}'

# Create task
curl -X POST http://localhost:5053/tasks \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"title":"Finish report","priority":"high","tags":["work","writing"]}'
```

## Schema

```sql
users        (id, username, email, password, created_at)
tasks        (id, user_id, title, description, status, priority, due_date, tags, created_at, updated_at)
task_logs    (id, task_id, user_id, action, old_value, new_value, created_at)
```

